1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,105
The same heat pump can save you money in Florida, and cost you hundreds more in Illinois.

2
00:00:05,225 --> 00:00:11,767
In Florida, heating a typical home costs about four hundred thirty dollars a year with a new gas furnace,

3
00:00:11,887 --> 00:00:14,213
and about three hundred forty with a heat pump.

4
00:00:14,333 --> 00:00:17,821
In Illinois, it's about five hundred fifty-five with gas,

5
00:00:17,941 --> 00:00:20,635
and about twelve hundred forty-five with a heat pump.

6
00:00:20,755 --> 00:00:22,952
The big difference is the price of gas.

7
00:00:23,072 --> 00:00:27,052
In Florida, it's about twenty-five dollars per thousand cubic feet.

8
00:00:27,172 --> 00:00:28,650
In Illinois, about eleven.

9
00:00:28,770 --> 00:00:31,227
Expensive gas makes the heat pump the winner.

10
00:00:31,346 --> 00:00:33,458
Cheap gas makes the furnace hard to beat.

11
00:00:33,578 --> 00:00:37,695
So before you choose, compare your own electricity and gas prices.

12
00:00:37,815 --> 00:00:40,854
Because the same heat pump can save you money in Florida…
